From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:58:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x: Keep the
 camera rails off for 2.5 s

The camera rails LDO1_M, LDO3_M and LDO7_B discharge slowly. When the
OV02C10 is powered again before they have, it stops answering on CCI
while its mode is written ("master 1 queue 0 timeout", "failed to set
mode").

Traced regulator events on a Yoga Slim 7x show restarts failing after
the rails were off for 1.2 s or less, and one failure in about 35
restarts with a 2 s off time. Give the three rails a 2.5 s off-on
delay.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261001-regulator-off-on-delay-v4-0-258ba9612da8@oss.qualcomm.com/
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts
index 19d9409..394300d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts
@@ -573,6 +573,7 @@ vreg_l7b_2p8: ldo7 {
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <2800000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <2800000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			regulator-off-on-delay-us = <2500000>;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l8b_3p0: ldo8 {
@@ -832,6 +833,7 @@ vreg_l1m_1p2: ldo1 {
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <1200000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1260000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			regulator-off-on-delay-us = <2500000>;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l2m_1p2: ldo2 {
@@ -846,6 +848,7 @@ vreg_l3m_1p8: ldo3 {
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1900000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			regulator-off-on-delay-us = <2500000>;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l4m_1p8: ldo4 {
